After some further messages from Rast and a review of the stats from
the alt.org server, I've come up with the following recommendation.
Basically two types of fighters and the spell casting wizard. If these
are OK, I'll also follow up with some type specific recommendations for
V, B, and W in other sections as well.
---

Previous versions of this guide has not recommending a starting
character type. However, after some feedback, I am making some
recommendations on the starting character that should help you make
further progress through the game.

*Valkyrie* - a female warrior starting with 16 (Human) or 18 (dwarf)
hit points, gaining up to 11 hit points for each experience level
increase. Magical power starts at one or two and grows the slowest of
any character type (along with Barbarian). The Valkyrie starts with
both long sword and dagger, some food, a +3 small shield, and a chance
of an oil lamp. This provides a good combination of hitting power and
armor. As a dwarf, you will have an easier time in the mines, but are
limited to the lawful alignment plus you cannot use a blessed genocide
on class h. A Valkyrie also starts with cold resistance and stealth,
gets speed at XL 7. At this time, according to the statistics on the
alt.org server, this is a popular choice and is second in total
ascensions on that server.

*Barbarian* - a warrior starting with 16 (Human) or 15 (orc) hit
points, gaining up to 12 hit points for each experience level increase.
Magical power starts at two or three and grows the slowest of any
character type (along with Valkyrie). The Barbarian starts with an axe
and sword, ring mail, some food, and a chance of an oil lamp. This also
is a good combination of hitting power and armor. As an orc, you have
infravision and can eat dogs, cats, and orcs without penalty, but are
limited in maximum abilities (e.g., strength). An orc is also limited
to the chaotic alignment - be careful to not anger your god since
reducing that armor is much harder for chaotic characters. A Barbarian
also starts with poison resistance, gains speed at XL 7 and stealth at
XL 15. At this time, according to the statistics on the alt.org server,
this is about half as popular as a Valkyrie but is third in total
ascensions on that server.

*Wizard* - a spell caster starting with 11 (elf, gnome, orc) or 12
(human) hit points, gaining up to 10 hit points for each experience
level increase. Magical power starts at five, six, or seven and grows
the fastest of any character type (along with Priest). The Wizard
starts with a quarterstaff, cloak of magic resistance, the force bolt
spell and a random lower level spell, random scrolls, random potions, a
random wand, and a chance of magic marker or blindfold. You must play
the wizard carefully in the early game due to low hit points, poor
armor, and lack of food (note also that spells cause hunger unless your
INT is 17 or more). But once past the early game, a wizard is one of
the most powerful characters. A Wizard starts only with racial
intrinsics (e.g., infravision) but gains warning at XL 15 and teleport
control at XL 17. At this time, according to the statistics on the
alt.org server, this is the most popular character type with most total
ascensions, but has a low ascension rate - likely due to early deaths.

One thing in common for these character types a relatively easy quest
nemesis; the quest artifacts for Valkyrie (Orb of Fate) and Wizard (Eye
of the Aethiopica) are excellent as well. I also ask you to do some
research on the benefits and drawbacks of each character type. Spoilers
to help you do this include...
 o the ability spoiler
(http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/abil-343.txt)
 o the hit point/power spoiler
(http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/hppw-343.txt)
 o the inventory spoiler
(http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/invt-343.txt)
 o the roles and races spoiler
(http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/331/rolerace.html)
 o the starting stats spoiler
(http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/stat-343.txt)
 o statistics of games played on the alt.org server
(http://alt.org/nethack/statnethack/statnethack.txt)

If you tend to have problems in the Gnomish Mines, you may want to pick
a dwarf or gnome. They have infravision (to see warm monsters in the
dark) and have more peaceful monsters in the Mines.

